      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "729715b7-9394-57ba-b473-7611d89ec49a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: King Conchobar, Cúchulainn, Queen Medb\n- Places: Ulster, Connacht, Cuailgne, Ireland, Lowland Scotland\n- Languages: Irish, Ulster Scots, Scots\n- Topics: Táin, Aikenhead surname\n\nFacts:\n- The Táin tells of the exploits of King Conchobar and his chief warrior Cúchulainn, who is called \"The Hound of Ulster.\"\n- The Táin tells of Queen Medb of Connacht invading Ulster in an attempt to capture the Brown Bull of Cuailgne.\n- Ulster is a province in the north of the island of Ireland.\n- Ulster is called \"Ulaidh\" or \"Cúige Uladh\" in Irish.\n- Ulster is called \"Ulstèr\" or \"Ulster\" in Ulster Scots.\n- Scots is a Germanic language variety spoken in Lowland Scotland and in parts of Ulster.\n- The local Scots dialect in parts of Ulster is known as Ulster Scots.\n- Aikenhead is a Scots language surname of medieval Scottish origin.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
